{"parentUuid":"08e046a9-3c2e-4e53-8696-90fc35a08369","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f3add2f7-ffac-43ca-818b-a54ab113212d","agentId":"a7b9a102584489b88","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UyiciMfQCQE9etQ7mkFzm1","type":"tool_result","content":"=== ./.claude/skills/mise/SKILL.md\n     1\t---\n     2\tname: mise\n     3\tdescription: Runs this repo's mise tasks and edits its mise config — use it before running, adding or changing a task, a tool pin, an env value or an alias.\n     4\t---\n     5\t\n     6\t# mise\n     7\t\n     8\tThis repo runs on mise: it pins the tools, holds the env values and runs the\n     9\ttasks.\n    10\t\n    11\t## Running tasks\n    12\t\n    13\t- Run every task as `mise run <task>`; discover them with `mise tasks`. Tasks\n    14\t  differ per repo, so never assume a task name the table below does not list.\n    15\t- Work locally under `MISE_ENV=dev`. `setup:all` refuses an unset `MISE_ENV`:\n    16\t  `MISE_ENV=dev mise run setup:all`.\n    17\t- `code:check:all`, `code:lint:all`, `code:format:all`, `setup:ai:all` and\n    18\t  `setup:deps:<verb>:all` run every subtask beside them; add a step by adding a\n    19\t  subtask file, never by editing an `all` task.\n    20\t\n    21\t## Where things live\n    22\t\n    23\t- `.config/miserc.toml` and `.config/mise.toml` hold settings and top-level\n    24\t  keys only.\n    25\t- `.config/mise/conf.d/<folder>/mise.toml` holds a folder's tools, env values,\n    26\t  tasks and aliases for every environment, `mise.<env>.toml` for one (`dev`,\n    27\t  `ci`, `test`). `_base/` and `ai/` are stackgen's, one folder per pack is the\n    28\t  pack's, and a folder named for a project is the repo's own.\n    29\t- `.config/mise/tasks/` holds the file-based tasks; `_scripts/` there is the\n    30\t  library they share.\n    31\t- `mise.local.toml` is this machine's, gitignored and never committed.\n    32\t- stackgen's tool-config renders `_base/`, `ai/`, each pack's folder and the\n    33\t  `all` tasks; a hand edit there is shown as a change on its next run. Put the\n    34\t  repo's own pins and values in a folder of its own.\n    35\t\n    36\t## Adding a tool\n    37\t\n    38\tPin it in exactly one folder. In `mise.dev.toml` write `version = \"latest\"`;\n    39\tin a file CI loads (`mise.toml`, `mise.ci.toml`, `mise.test.toml`) write the\n    40\texact version. Then run `mise install` — never a bare `mise use`, which writes\n    41\tthe top-level config this layout keeps settings-only.\n    42\t\n    43\t## Tasks\n    44\t\n    45\t| Task | Description |\n    46\t| ---- | ----------- |\n    47\t@@#each TASKS@@\n    48\t| `@@.name@@` | @@.description@@ |\n    49\t@@/each@@\n=== ./.config/claude-status.json\n     1\t{\n     2\t  \"$schema\": \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/virajp/claude-status/main/schemas/claude-status.schema.json\",\n     3\t  \"projectName\": \"@@PROJECT_NAME@@\"\n     4\t}\n=== ./.config/git-conventional-commits.yaml\n     1\t---\n     2\t# The commit convention: the `commit-msg` hook enforces it, and the changelog reads it.\n     3\t\n     4\tconvention:\n     5\t  # Ten types, and no more.\n     6\t  commitTypes:\n     7\t    - feat # a new capability a user can observe. Bumps the minor version.\n     8\t    - fix # a defect in a shipped capability, not in one added this branch.\n     9\t    - perf # same behaviour, measurably cheaper. Say what was measured.\n    10\t    - refactor # neither fixes nor adds — including pure formatting changes.\n    11\t    - revert # undoes an earlier commit; name it in the body.\n    12\t    - test # tests only. A test written alongside a fix belongs to the fix.\n    13\t    - ops # tooling, config, dependencies, CI, release mechanics.\n    14\t    - docs # prose: README, guides, specifications, design documents.\n    15\t    - merge # a merge commit. Written by the merge task, rarely by hand.\n    16\t    - wip # work in progress. Never survives a merge; excluded from notes.\n    17\t\n    18\t  # One scope per project id.\n    19\t  # A scope that stops existing stays in stackgen.yaml's `scopes`: deleting it invalidates its commits.\n    20\t@@#if SCOPES@@\n    21\t  commitScopes:\n    22\t@@#each SCOPES@@\n    23\t    - @@.@@\n    24\t@@/each@@\n    25\t@@#else@@\n    26\t  commitScopes: []\n    27\t@@/if@@\n    28\t\n    29\t  featureCommitTypes:\n    30\t    - feat\n    31\t\n    32\t  # A repo that namespaces its tags per component narrows this to that prefix.\n    33\t  releaseTagGlobPattern: \"*\"\n    34\t\n    35\tchangelog:\n    36\t  # test, ops, docs, merge and wip are deliberately absent from the notes.\n    37\t  commitTypes:\n    38\t    - feat\n    39\t    - fix\n    40\t    - perf\n    41\t    - refactor\n    42\t    - revert\n    43\t\n    44\t  includeInvalidCommits: false\n    45\t\n    46\t  # Also catches `wip` commits written before the convention.\n    47\t  commitIgnoreRegexPattern: '^[wW][iI][pP]\\b'\n    48\t\n    49\t  headlines:\n    50\t    feat: Features\n    51\t    fix: Bug Fixes\n    52\t    perf: Performance Improvements\n    53\t    refactor: Refactors\n    54\t    revert: Reverts\n    55\t    breakingChange: BREAKING CHANGES\n    56\t@@#if REPO_URL@@\n    57\t\n    58\t  # The changelog links, from `origin`.\n    59\t  commitUrl: @@REPO_URL@@/commit/%commit%\n    60\t  commitRangeUrl: @@REPO_URL@@/compare/%from%...%to%?diff=split\n    61\t  issueRegexPattern: \"#[0-9]+\"\n    62\t  issueUrl: @@REPO_URL@@/issues/%issue%\n    63\t@@/if@@\n=== ./.config/mise/conf.d/_base/mise.ci.toml\n     1\t@@#if NODE@@\n     2\t[settings]\n     3\t# mise's bundled Node release-key import (gpg --import) fails on the Ubuntu CI\n     4\t# runner's gpg with \"no valid OpenPGP data found\", aborting `mise install`. The\n     5\t# same mise version verifies fine on macOS, so it is a mise-on-Linux bug, not a\n     6\t# version issue — pinning does not help. Disable only the gpg signature check in\n     7\t# CI; the Node tarball is still SHA256-checksum verified (node.verify). Local dev\n     8\t# (mise.toml) keeps full gpg verification.\n     9\tnode.gpg_verify = false\n    10\t@@/if@@\n=== ./.config/mise/conf.d/_base/mise.dev.toml\n     1\t# The developer laptop's base — loaded when MISE_ENV includes dev. Dev tools stay on latest.\n     2\t\n     3\t[settings]\n     4\t# Python, pipx, uv settings\n     5\t# every pipx: tool installs through uv\n     6\tpipx.uvx            = true\n     7\tpython.compile      = false\n     8\tpython.uv_venv_auto = \"create|source\"\n     9\t@@#if NODE@@\n    10\t@@#else@@\n    11\t\n    12\t# The tool-config script runs on node; a node repo pins it in mise.toml instead.\n    13\t[tools.node]\n    14\tversion = \"latest\"\n    15\t\n    16\t[tools.pnpm]\n    17\tdepends = [ \"node\" ]\n    18\tversion = \"latest\"\n    19\t@@/if@@\n    20\t\n    21\t# mise's pipx backend installs through uv, and uv needs a Python >= 3.10 to lock graphifyy's dependencies.\n    22\t[tools.python]\n    23\tversion = \"latest\"\n    24\t\n    25\t[tools.uv]\n    26\tdepends = [ \"python\" ]\n    27\tversion = \"latest\"\n    28\t\n    29\t[tools.\"pre-commit\"]\n    30\tdepends = [ \"python\", \"uv\" ]\n    31\tuvx     = true\n    32\tversion = \"latest\"\n    33\t\n    34\t# OSV Scanner is a tool for scanning open source vulnerabilities.\n    35\t[tools.osv-scanner]\n    36\tversion = \"latest\"\n    37\t\n    38\t# Grype is a vulnerability scanner for container images\n    39\t# and filesystems\n    40\t[tools.grype]\n    41\tversion = \"latest\"\n    42\t\n    43\t# Gitleaks is a SAST tool for detecting hardcoded secrets like\n    44\t# passwords, API keys, and tokens in git repositories\n    45\t[tools.gitleaks]\n    46\tversion = \"latest\"\n    47\t\n    48\t# Dprint is a code formatter for various programming languages\n    49\t[tools.dprint]\n    50\tversion = \"latest\"\n    51\t\n    52\t# Taplo is a code formatter for TOML files\n    53\t[tools.taplo]\n    54\tdepends = [ \"dprint\" ]\n    55\tversion = \"latest\"\n    56\t\n    57\t# Shell and workflow gates: `code:{format,lint}:shell` and `code:lint:workflows`.\n    58\t[tools.shellcheck]\n    59\tversion = \"latest\"\n    60\t\n    61\t[tools.shfmt]\n    62\tversion = \"latest\"\n    63\t\n    64\t[tools.actionlint]\n    65\tversion = \"latest\"\n    66\t\n    67\t# The house linter, run by `code:lint:house`.\n    68\t[tools.\"npm:@askviraj/linter\"]\n    69\tallow_low_downloads = true\n    70\tversion             = \"latest\"\n    71\t\n    72\t[shell_alias]\n    73\tprecommit = \"mise run code:precommit\"\n    74\tsetup     = \"mise run setup:all\"\n    75\tworktrees = \"mise run code:worktrees\"\n    76\t@@#each MEMBER_ENTRIES@@\n    77\tsetup-@@.slug@@ = \"mise run setup:all --@@.slug@@\"\n    78\t@@/each@@\n    79\t\n    80\t[env]\n    81\tPRE_COMMIT_HOME = \"$HOME/.cache/pre-commit\"\n    82\t\n    83\t# Python (uv)\n    84\tUV_NO_CACHE          = true\n    85\tUV_NO_MANAGED_PYTHON = true\n    86\tUV_PYTHON_DOWNLOADS  = \"never\"\n=== ./.config/mise/conf.d/_base/mise.toml\n     1\t# Every repo's base, loaded in every MISE_ENV. A tool is pinned in exactly one conf.d folder.\n     2\t@@#if NODE@@\n     3\t\n     4\t[settings]\n     5\t# NodeJS settings\n     6\tnode.compile        = false\n     7\tnpm.package_manager = \"pnpm\"\n     8\t\n     9\t# Node has good backward compatibility: node and pnpm stay on latest even where CI loads them.\n    10\t[tools.node]\n    11\tversion = \"latest\"\n    12\t\n    13\t[tools.pnpm]\n    14\tdepends = [ \"node\" ]\n    15\tversion = \"latest\"\n    16\t@@/if@@\n    17\t\n    18\t[tasks.init]\n    19\t# In the base, not dev: `setup:all` depends on it, and CI needs the task files executable too.\n    20\tdescription = \"Initialize mise tasks\"\n    21\tdir         = \"{{exec(command='git rev-parse --show-toplevel')}}\"\n    22\thide        = true\n    23\trun         = \"find .config/mise/tasks/ -name '*' -type f -not -path '*/*.env' -exec chmod 755 {} \\\\;\"\n    24\t\n    25\t[env]\n    26\t@@#if NODE@@\n    27\t_.path = { path = \"node_modules/.bin\", tools = true }\n    28\t\n    29\t@@/if@@\n    30\t# A literal: never derive it at load time, since a linked worktree's folder is named for its branch.\n    31\tREPO_NAME = \"@@REPO_NAME@@\"\n    32\t\n    33\t# `direct` merges locally, `pr` opens a pull request.\n    34\tMERGE_MODEL_DEVELOP = \"@@MERGE_MODEL_DEVELOP@@\"\n    35\tMERGE_MODEL_MAIN    = \"@@MERGE_MODEL_MAIN@@\"\n    36\t\n    37\t# Member repo paths, space-separated; empty when the members are submodules.\n    38\tMEMBERS = \"@@MEMBERS_SPACED@@\"\n=== ./.config/mise/conf.d/ai/mise.dev.toml\n     1\t# AI Tools\n     2\t[tools.jq]\n     3\tversion = \"latest\"\n     4\t\n     5\t[tools.yq]\n     6\tversion = \"latest\"\n     7\t\n     8\t[tools.\"pipx:mempalace\"]\n     9\tdepends = [ \"python\", \"uv\" ]\n    10\tuvx     = true\n    11\tversion = \"latest\"\n    12\t\n    13\t[tools.\"pipx:graphifyy\"]\n    14\tdepends = [ \"python\", \"uv\" ]\n    15\tuvx     = true\n    16\tversion = \"latest\"\n    17\t\n    18\t[env]\n    19\t# Mempalace Backend (common across repos)\n    20\tMEMPALACE_BACKEND               = \"qdrant\"\n    21\tMEMPALACE_EMBEDDING_DEVICE      = \"auto\"\n    22\tMEMPALACE_EMBEDDING_MODEL       = \"minilm\"\n    23\tMEMPALACE_MAX_BACKUPS           = 4\n    24\tMEMPALACE_MCP_ALLOW_PEER_WRITER = 1\n    25\tMEMPALACE_MCP_IDLE_HOURS        = 0\n    26\tMEMPALACE_QDRANT_URL            = \"http://127.0.0.1:6333\"\n    27\t\n    28\t# Palace path for storing local data\n    29\tMEMPALACE_PALACE_PATH = \"~/.local/share/mempalace/@@REPO_NAME@@\"\n=== ./.config/mise/tasks/code/check/all\n     1\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\n     2\t\n     3\t#MISE description=\"Run the repo's checks — every code:check subtask\"\n     4\t#MISE dir=\"{{ config_root }}\"\n     5\t\n     6\t#USAGE flag \"--debug\" help=\"emit debug logs\"\n     7\t#USAGE arg \"[files]\" var=#true help=\"files to check (default: the whole repo)\"\n     8\t\n     9\tset -euo pipefail\n    10\t# shellcheck source=/dev/null\n    11\tsource \"${MISE_PROJECT_ROOT}/.config/mise/tasks/_scripts/helpers\"\n    12\t\n    13\t# Rendered by stackgen tool-config: one call per subtask under code/check/, re-rendered whenever a pack adds or removes one.\n    14\t@@#if CHECK_SUBTASKS@@\n    15\t\n    16\tfiles=()\n    17\teval \"files+=(${usage_files:-})\"\n    18\t\n    19\targs=()\n    20\t[[ \"${usage_debug:-false}\" == \"true\" ]] && args+=(--debug)\n    21\t@@#each CHECK_SUBTASKS@@\n    22\t\n    23\tmise run code:check:@@.@@ ${args[@]+\"${args[@]}\"} ${files[@]+\"${files[@]}\"}\n    24\t@@/each@@\n    25\t@@#else@@\n    26\t\n    27\tprint_yellow \"code:check: nothing to run — this repo has no code:check:<name> subtask.\"\n    28\t@@/if@@\n=== ./.config/mise/tasks/code/format/all\n     1\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\n     2\t\n     3\t#MISE description=\"Format the repo's files — every code:format subtask\"\n     4\t#MISE dir=\"{{ config_root }}\"\n     5\t\n     6\t#USAGE flag \"--debug\" help=\"emit debug logs\"\n     7\t#USAGE flag \"--fix\" help=\"apply fixes\"\n     8\t#USAGE arg \"[files]\" var=#true help=\"files to format (default: the whole repo)\"\n     9\t\n    10\tset -euo pipefail\n    11\t# shellcheck source=/dev/null\n    12\tsource \"${MISE_PROJECT_ROOT}/.config/mise/tasks/_scripts/helpers\"\n    13\t\n    14\t# Rendered by stackgen tool-config: one call per subtask under code/format/, re-rendered whenever a pack adds or removes one.\n    15\t@@#if FORMAT_SUBTASKS@@\n    16\t\n    17\tfiles=()\n    18\teval \"files+=(${usage_files:-})\"\n    19\t\n    20\targs=()\n    21\t[[ \"${usage_debug:-false}\" == \"true\" ]] && args+=(--debug)\n    22\t[[ \"${usage_fix:-false}\" == \"true\" ]] && args+=(--fix)\n    23\t@@#each FORMAT_SUBTASKS@@\n    24\t\n    25\tmise run code:format:@@.@@ ${args[@]+\"${args[@]}\"} ${files[@]+\"${files[@]}\"}\n    26\t@@/each@@\n    27\t@@#else@@\n    28\t\n    29\tprint_yellow \"code:format: nothing to run — this repo has no code:format:<name> subtask.\"\n    30\t@@/if@@\n=== ./.config/mise/tasks/code/lint/all\n     1\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\n     2\t\n     3\t#MISE description=\"Lint the repo's files — every code:lint subtask\"\n     4\t#MISE dir=\"{{ config_root }}\"\n     5\t\n     6\t#USAGE flag \"--debug\" help=\"emit debug logs\"\n     7\t#USAGE flag \"--fix\" help=\"apply fixes\"\n     8\t#USAGE arg \"[files]\" var=#true help=\"files to lint (default: the whole repo)\"\n     9\t\n    10\tset -euo pipefail\n    11\t# shellcheck source=/dev/null\n    12\tsource \"${MISE_PROJECT_ROOT}/.config/mise/tasks/_scripts/helpers\"\n    13\t\n    14\t# Rendered by stackgen tool-config: one call per subtask under code/lint/, re-rendered whenever a pack adds or removes one.\n    15\t@@#if LINT_SUBTASKS@@\n    16\t\n    17\tfiles=()\n    18\teval \"files+=(${usage_files:-})\"\n    19\t\n    20\targs=()\n    21\t[[ \"${usage_debug:-false}\" == \"true\" ]] && args+=(--debug)\n    22\t[[ \"${usage_fix:-false}\" == \"true\" ]] && args+=(--fix)\n    23\t@@#each LINT_SUBTASKS@@\n    24\t\n    25\tmise run code:lint:@@.@@ ${args[@]+\"${args[@]}\"} ${files[@]+\"${files[@]}\"}\n    26\t@@/each@@\n    27\t@@#else@@\n    28\t\n    29\tprint_yellow \"code:lint: nothing to run — this repo has no code:lint:<name> subtask.\"\n    30\t@@/if@@\n=== ./.config/mise/tasks/setup/ai/all\n     1\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\n     2\t\n     3\t#MISE description=\"Reconcile the AI tooling — every setup:ai subtask\"\n     4\t#MISE hide=true\n     5\t\n     6\tset -euo pipefail\n     7\t# shellcheck source=/dev/null\n     8\tsource \"${MISE_PROJECT_ROOT}/.config/mise/tasks/_scripts/helpers\"\n     9\t\n    10\t# Rendered by stackgen tool-config: one call per subtask under setup/ai/, re-rendered whenever a pack adds or removes one.\n    11\t@@#if AI_SUBTASKS@@\n    12\t@@#each AI_SUBTASKS@@\n    13\t\n    14\tmise run setup:ai:@@.@@\n    15\t@@/each@@\n    16\t@@#else@@\n    17\t\n    18\tprint_yellow \"setup:ai: nothing to run — this repo has no setup:ai:<name> subtask.\"\n    19\t@@/if@@\n=== ./.config/mise/tasks/setup/all\n     1\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\n     2\t\n     3\t#MISE description=\"Set up everything this repo needs on your machine\"\n     4\t#MISE depends=[\"init\"]\n     5\t\n     6\t#USAGE flag \"--all\" help=\"Also set up every member project\"\n     7\t\n     8\t# One flag per member repo, named by its slug.\n     9\t@@#each MEMBER_ENTRIES@@\n    10\t#USAGE flag \"--@@.slug@@\" help=\"Set up the @@.path@@ project\"\n    11\t@@/each@@\n    12\t\n    13\tset -euo pipefail\n    14\t# shellcheck source=/dev/null\n    15\tsource \"${MISE_PROJECT_ROOT}/.config/mise/tasks/_scripts/helpers\"\n    16\t\n    17\t# MISE_ENV decides which conf.d files load; guessing it is wrong.\n    18\tif [ -z \"${MISE_ENV:-}\" ]; then\n    19\t  print_error \"MISE_ENV is unset. On a developer machine run: MISE_ENV=dev mise run setup:all\"\n    20\t  exit 1\n    21\tfi\n    22\t\n    23\t# Idempotent and non-destructive: it installs the pins and moves none.\n    24\tprint_header \"Setting up the toolchain ...\"\n    25\tmise run setup:mise\n    26\t\n    27\tprint_header \"Setting up secrets ...\"\n    28\tmise run setup:secrets\n    29\t\n    30\t@@#if EXTERNAL@@\n    31\tprint_header \"Starting external services ...\"\n    32\tmise run setup:external:start\n    33\t\n    34\t@@/if@@\n    35\tprint_header \"Setting up dependencies ...\"\n    36\tmise run setup:deps:all\n    37\t\n    38\tprint_header \"Setting up commit hooks ...\"\n    39\tmise run setup:precommit\n    40\t\n    41\tprint_header \"Setting up AI tooling ...\"\n    42\tmise run setup:ai:all\n    43\t\n    44\t# Members only on request — `--all`, or a member's own `--<slug>` — each running its OWN task library\n    45\t# from inside it, so its own miserc.toml is read. The slug is the member folder's name, slugified as the\n    46\t# flags above w