{"parentUuid":"6f1b04df-9ff7-472a-bba5-98fa529258e2","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a7b9a102584489b88","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfiiz1rjbNXwnWrnQEwwe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3722,"cache_read_input_tokens":220105,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3722,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7024,"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfiiz12PJ7Up2oQLCFDsm","attributionSkill":"code-review","type":"assistant","uuid":"21b9f2d4-1dae-4092-a53c-eee6c951d692","timestamp":"2026-10-05T07:50:27.888Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/virajpatel/Projects/github.com/virajp/claude-plugins/.worktrees/2026-10-05-tool-config-templates","sessionId":"69f6d805-2cf4-410f-bb9a-f18a900e1285","version":"2.1.289","gitBranch":"2026-10-05-tool-config-templates"}
{"parentUuid":"21b9f2d4-1dae-4092-a53c-eee6c951d692","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a7b9a102584489b88","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfiiz1rjbNXwnWrnQEwwe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found 10 problems on `2026-10-05-tool-config-templates`. The most serious is that the packs' dependency-install subtasks and several format and lint subtasks were deleted instead of moved. I had no access to the U6 and U7 (pending) docs, so I did not count stale task names in prose as findings.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"file\": \"plugins/stackgen/stacks/package-manager/pnpm/templates/.config/mise/conf.d/pnpm/mise.dev.toml\",\n    \"line\": 1,\n    \"summary\": \"U3 deleted the packs' task overlays without moving them to subtasks, despite E10 and edit 3 of its unit: no setup/deps/<verb>/<slug> exists for flutter, swiftui, swift, pnpm or uv, and the flutter dart, ruff and pnpm sort-package-json format/lint subtasks are gone. This file's comment even names a code:format:pnpm task that does not exist.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"In a pnpm, uv, flutter or swift repo, setup:deps:install:all renders the 'nothing to run' branch, so `mise run setup:all` and `setup:worktree --frozen` never run pnpm install, uv sync or flutter pub get. code:format:all and code:lint:all never run dart format, ruff or sort-package-json, so the pre-commit format and lint hooks silently stop enforcing those tools.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"plugins/stackgen/skills/tool-config/scripts/tool-config.mjs\",\n    \"line\": 274,\n    \"summary\": \"writeFiles() writes paths one at a time with no try/restore. A mkdirSync that fails halfway (EEXIST/ENOTDIR) escapes as an internal fault and leaves earlier files overwritten; restore() is only built after the loop and only called on formatter or validate failures.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A repo shaped by the previous release has .config/mise/tasks/code/format as a file. `all` writes .config/dprint.json, .config/mise.toml, _scripts/* and code/all, then mkdirSync('.config/mise/tasks/code/format') throws EEXIST. The script exits 1 with a half-written tree and nothing put back. Preview could not show this, because safe()/disk() treat ENOTDIR as absent.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"plugins/stackgen/skills/tool-config/assets/.config/mise/tasks/code/graph\",\n    \"line\": 69,\n    \"summary\": \"The PID-liveness and takeover guards were replaced with a lock-dir mtime check. A live lock older than 30 minutes is now deleted, and two runs that both see a stale lock can each rm -rf and re-mkdir it.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A large repo's rebuild, now up to two full `graphify update` passes under one lock, takes over 30 minutes; the next commit's hook removes the live lock and starts a second concurrent `graphify update .` writing the same graphify-out/. Or: hooks A and B both see a stale lock, A re-mkdirs it, B's rm -rf removes A's fresh lock and B also proceeds.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"plugins/stackgen/skills/tool-config/scripts/lib/render.mjs\",\n    \"line\": 283,\n    \"summary\": \"subtaskNames() keeps every file directly in a subtask folder except `all`. Unlike taskNames() it does not skip dot-files or non-task files, so they get rendered into the …:all tasks as subtask calls.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Finder drops .config/mise/tasks/code/lint/.DS_Store. The next render writes `mise run code:lint:.DS_Store …` into code/lint/all, which fails with task-not-found, so the pre-commit lint hook and code:all fail on every commit.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"plugins/stackgen/skills/tool-config/assets/.config/pre-commit-config.yaml\",\n    \"line\": 93,\n    \"summary\": \"uv's lock check moved from a hook gated on `files: (^|.*/)pyproject\\\\.toml$` to the always_run, pass_filenames:false `check` hook. The changed-manifest gate was dropped.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"In a Python repo every commit, including docs-only ones, runs code:check:all, which runs `mise x -- uv lock --check` for every uv.lock. Commits get slower, can need index/network access, and fail offline where the old hook was skipped.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"plugins/stackgen/skills/tool-config/scripts/tool-config.mjs\",\n    \"line\": 697,\n    \"summary\": \"Rows are answered independently, so a pack-remove can leave a re-rendered …:all task inconsistent with the subtask deletions it was computed against.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"`pack-remove --slug swiftlint` shows a delete row for code/lint/swiftlint and a write row for code/lint/all. Answering r1:ok and r2:keep-existing deletes the subtask but keeps the old lint:all that still runs `mise run code:lint:swiftlint`, so the lint hook fails on every commit.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"plugins/stackgen/skills/tool-config/scripts/tool-config.mjs\",\n    \"line\": 466,\n    \"summary\": \"cmdUpgrade calls runner.latest(), which throws a RefusalError when `mise latest` fails. One unresolvable tool therefore aborts the whole upgrade, even though the `!isExact(to)` check right after it shows the intent was to skip such a pin.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A repo pins aqua:realm/SwiftLint and fnox exactly in CI-loaded files. `mise latest` for one backend fails (rate limit, offline registry, a tool with no releases listing), so `upgrade` exits 2 and no other pin moves.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"plugins/stackgen/skills/tool-config/scripts/tool-config.mjs\",\n    \"line\": 308,\n    \"summary\": \"place() deletes a target whose source renders empty before the filledSlot() check, so the `#PLACEHOLDER never overwrites a filled slot` rule does not protect a repo-written setup/external task when EXTERNAL turns false.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A repo replaces the setup/external/start placeholder with its own docker-compose script, then runs `all --external false`. The render is empty, so the repo's hand-written start, stop and pull scripts are offered as delete rows; an `ok` answer loses them.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"scripts/src/check.ts\",\n    \"line\": 676,\n    \"summary\": \"The checker requires a pack subtask's leaf to be the pack slug, but does not require a pack's templates/ mise files to sit under conf.d/<slug>/. pack-remove deletes only conf.d/<slug>/ and slug-named subtasks.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A pack ships templates/.config/mise/conf.d/_base/mise.toml or conf.d/<other>/mise.toml. The checker passes. `pack` overwrites the universal base or another pack's folder, and `pack-remove` never deletes it, leaving orphaned pins. The fix is to apply the same slug rule to the templates/ conf.d folder.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"plugins/stackgen/skills/tool-config/scripts/lib/render.mjs\",\n    \"line\": 257,\n    \"summary\": \"valueNames() refuses empty and duplicate member slugs but not a slug equal to `all`, which collides with setup:all's own `--all` usage flag and usage_all variable.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"`all --members apps/all` renders `#USAGE flag \\\"--all\\\"` twice in setup/all. mise's usage spec rejects the duplicate flag, or it is read as 'set up every member', so `MISE_ENV=dev mise run setup:all` breaks.\"\n  }\n]\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3722,"cache_read_input_tokens":220105,"output_tokens":2695,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":17},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3722},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2695,"cache_read_input_tokens":220105,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3722,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3722,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"api